# runtime/ADDRESS_CASTS
#
# Functions that convert a pointer to an integer as address arithmetic, address ordering or a
# kernel token.  Checked by `just runtime-word-casts` (scripts/runtime_word_casts.py;
# docs/string-header-invariant-v0.md §4.2, §4.3).
#
# One `file:name` per line (file as `runtime/x.c`; a same-named static in another file is not
# covered), a `# reason` on the SAME line.  A listed function is checked for exactly this:
#   - A1: every pointer-to-integer cast in it has destination type spelled `uintptr_t`.
#   - A2: it converts no `uintptr_t` or `intptr_t` value to a signed integer type of 64 bits or
#     more (`long`, `long long`, `int64_t`, `__int128`), by cast or implicitly.  Conversions to
#     unsigned or narrower types (`size_t`, `int`) are fine.
#   - It does not return an integer type of 64 bits or more (`long`, `long long`, `__int128`, or
#     a typedef of one: `uintptr_t`, `size_t`, ...) and takes no pointer to one (an out-param).
#     A by-value 64-bit parameter is fine.
#   - A name with no definition, or no pointer-to-integer cast on the host platform, is stale
#     and fails the gate.
# Nothing else is checked.  Not seen: an address laundered through arithmetic into a non-address
# type, `memcpy`, union punning, or reinterpretation through a `void*` (docs/gates.md).
# A function that needs to convert an address to a signed 64-bit integer cannot be listed here:
# it leaves through sprout_str_word or sprout_ptr_word.
#
# The AST holds one platform's #ifdef branches.  An entry may carry one tag, `darwin` or `linux`,
# after the name: it is then allowed and checked only on that host and ignored on the other, so
# a cast that appears in that function on the other host fails the gate.  An
# untagged entry is checked on every host and must have a cast on both.

runtime/sprout_runtime.c:arena_contains       # range test of an address against the arena
runtime/sprout_runtime.c:region_find          # address -> region; index arithmetic on the base
runtime/sprout_runtime.c:region_find_slow     # binary search of the region table by address
runtime/sprout_runtime.c:open_new_region      # orders the new region into the table by address
runtime/sprout_runtime.c:region_table_insert  # sorted insert by address; keeps the heap span
runtime/sprout_runtime.c:sprout_fl_entry_cmp  # qsort comparator: free-list entries by address
runtime/sprout_poll.c:poll_tag_timer linux    # epoll: sets bit 0 of a token; returns a pointer
runtime/sprout_poll.c:poll_untag linux        # epoll: reads and clears bit 0; returns a pointer
